==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|nation|ist|lang=en}}, from {{m|en|nationism}}, {{w|Joshua Fishman}}, 1968.<ref>Fishman, J.A. 1968. Nationality–nationalism and nation–nationism. Fishman, J.A.; Ferguson, C.A.; Das Gupta, J., ed. ''Language problems of developing nations.'' John Wiley & Sons, New York, NY, USA. pp. 39–51.</ref>

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{label|en|sociolinguistics}} A language used for the day-to-day functioning of government – official forms, intra-government communication.
# {{misspelling of|nationalist|lang=en}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|nationism}}

